<title>USA: OHM wins $50-$75 million contract.</title>
<headline>OHM wins $50-$75 million contract.</headline>
<dateline>FINDLAY, Ohio 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>OHM Corp said Monday it won a contract estimated at $50 to $75 million from the Department of the Army Corps of Engineers to provide hazardous waste cleanup services at sites in the United States and internationally.</p>
<p>The contract covers one year and may be extended for four additional one-year options, OHM said in a news release.</p>
<p>OHM has worked with the Corps of Engineers on similar contracts since 1989.</p>
<p>Shares of OHM were trading up 1/16 to 8-7/16.</p>
<p>		   ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
